---
// Home. All copy is from the brief (EdTerm_Site_Brief.md) or approved by the owner; see CLAUDE.md before editing.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import StackDiagram from '../components/StackDiagram.astro';
import LoopBlock from '../components/LoopBlock.astro';
import ProofCard from '../components/ProofCard.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';

const link = 'font-semibold text-purple-700 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-purple-500';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="EdTerm — The Human Wisdom Database"
  description="EdTerm is building the world's first Human Wisdom Database — preserving lived human experience as structured, searchable knowledge available to everyone, everywhere, forever."
>
  <!-- Hero A headline (brief) + owner-approved supporting line -->
  <Hero
    label="Healthcare data infrastructure"
    headline="The future of healthcare is data-driven. The question is what data AI is actually learning from."
  >
    <p>
      EdTerm is a healthcare data infrastructure company building the reasoning layer that completes what EHRs and
      genomic databases cannot capture: how experienced clinicians reason through a decision before it’s lost to
      turnover. Everyday expertise is walking out the door.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Original Hero A subtext, unchanged -->
  <Section tone="white" layout="stack">
    <p class="text-lead">
      Right now it's learning from outcomes and records. But the judgment, the ethics, the human touch that separates
      great clinical care from efficient clinical processing — that's not in the dataset. If we don't put it there
      intentionally, AI systems will optimize around it. EdTerm captures it.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <!-- The stack: EHR/imaging → genomics → reasoning layer (Hero B lines) -->
  <section class="bg-paper py-section" aria-labelledby="stack-heading">
    <div class="container-site grid-12 items-center gap-y-12">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
        <h2 id="stack-heading" class="text-h2 font-bold text-purple-700">
          The capture side doesn't compete with medical data. It completes it.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-(--container-prose)">
          Patient data tells you what happened. Genomic data tells you what's possible. The wisdom layer tells you how
          experienced clinicians interpret all of it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6"><a href="/reasoning-layer" class={link}>Explore the reasoning layer</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
        <StackDiagram />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Two equal-weight sections, one source: joined by the loop line -->
  <LoopBlock heading="The data layer" tone="white" position="first" id="data-layer">
    <p>Clinical AI, decision support and training systems can reference expert reasoning, not only outcomes.</p>
    <p>
      AI systems trained on clinical outcomes can tell you what happened to similar patients. They cannot tell you how
      an experienced clinician would read the same presentation.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/health-systems" class={link}>For health systems</a></p>
  </LoopBlock>

  <LoopBlock heading="The education loop" tone="paper" position="last" id="education-loop">
    <p>The same captured knowledge returns to medical and nursing education.</p>
    <p>Practitioner knowledge returns to curriculum, so the next cohort trains on what practitioners actually learned.</p>
    <p><a href="/education" class={link}>For education</a></p>
    <Fragment slot="close">Both loops close from the same source.</Fragment>
  </LoopBlock>

  <!-- Credibility strip -->
  <Section tone="deep" layout="stack" heading="Evidence">
    <ul slot="wide" class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <li>
        <ProofCard title="Peer-reviewed methodology" text="Double-blind peer review through IAFOR." href="/evidence#peer-review" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <ProofCard
          title="IRB-approved study"
          text="An IRB-approved study through Lindenwood University, now open for participants."
          href="/evidence#lindenwood-study"
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <ProofCard
          title="18th Annual Asian Conference on Education (ACE2026), Tokyo, 2026"
          text="Presented the Wisdom Journalism methodology as curriculum design."
          href="/evidence#ace2026"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <!-- The single call to action -->
  <CTA heading="Early Access" buttonLabel="Request early access" />
</BaseLayout>
